# --- Local agentic / editor tooling (per-developer, intentionally untracked) --
# The project-level setup that IS shared lives in docker-compose*.yml, docs/,
# scripts/ and CLAUDE.md. Everything below is whatever agent or editor each
# developer happens to use, and is deliberately not imposed on the team.
.claude/
.agents/
.agent-native/
.vscode/

# .cursor is per-developer EXCEPT its rules, which are project standards rather
# than tooling preference: `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` points Cursor at AGENTS.md and
# docs/full-stack-engineering.md, so a Cursor user who does not get them does
# not get the conventions either.
#
# Spelled out rather than `.cursor/` + a negation, because git cannot re-include
# a file whose parent directory is excluded — the negation would silently do
# nothing. This was already the de facto state: full-stack-engineering.mdc is
# tracked, so `.cursor/` never applied to it, while any NEW rule file was
# silently unaddable without `git add -f`.
.cursor/*
!.cursor/rules/
.cursor/rules/*
!.cursor/rules/*.mdc
.mcp.json
opencode.json
agent-native.json
skills-lock.json
.opencode/

# AGENTS.md is the exception: it is a TRACKED symlink to CLAUDE.md, so every
# assistant reads the same instructions. Keep it out of the ignores above.

# --- Local dev seed data -----------------------------------------------------
# Database dumps used to seed the local stack. These contain real business data
# and must never be committed. See seed/README.md and `npm run seed`.
seed/*
!seed/README.md

# --- Git worktrees -----------------------------------------------------------
# `npm run worktree -- new` creates linked checkouts in here. They are full
# working trees of this same repository, so they must never be added to it.
# Anchored with a leading slash: only the one at the repo root, not any
# directory named "worktrees" elsewhere. See docs/worktrees.md.
/worktrees/

# --- Playwright ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts: the HTML report, traces, and the last-run marker. Regenerated by
# `npm run e2e`; `npm run e2e:report` opens the report locally.
Frontend/playwright-report/
Frontend/test-results/
